  "live_records": {
    "q-256827": {
      "dom_id": "step-q256827",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4{x}^{2}$ in the interval $[-2,2].$ Calculate the second iteration of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization starting from the point ${x}_{0}=2.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson process for optimization is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}{{f}^{″}({x}_{n})},\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ and ${f}^{″}({x}_{n})$ are the first and second derivatives of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n},$ respectively.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-4{x}^{2})^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-8x, \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-8x)^{′}=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{n})+{x}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{n})-8{x}_{n}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{n})-{x}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{n})-8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{0})+{x}_{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{0})-8{x}_{0}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{0})-{x}_{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{0})-8} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2)-8(2)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2)-8} \\\\  & =0.505\\,007…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1})-8{x}_{1}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}_{1})-{x}_{1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}_{1})-8} \\\\  & =(0.505\\,007…)-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.505\\,007…)+(0.505\\,007…)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.505\\,007…)-8(0.505\\,007…)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0.505\\,007…)-(0.505\\,007…)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0.505\\,007…)-8} \\\\  & ≈0.025,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
