    "q-256858": {
      "dom_id": "step-q256858",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Suppose we wish to find a critical point of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2}$ in the interval $[0.5,1].$ Calculate the first two iterations of the Newton-Raphson process for optimization starting at the point ${x}_{0}=1.$ Round your answers to three decimal places.\n\n${x}_{1}≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$,\\,{x}_{2}≈$\n{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "The Newton-Raphson process for optimization is\n\n$$\n{x}_{n+1}={x}_{n}-\\frac{{f}^{′}({x}_{n})}{{f}^{″}({x}_{n})},\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}^{′}({x}_{n})$ and ${f}^{″}({x}_{n})$ are the first and second derivatives of $f(x)$ evaluated at ${x}_{n},$ respectively.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-{x}^{2})^{′}=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)-2x, \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)-2x)^{′}=-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our Newton-Raphson formula is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{n+1} & ={x}_{n}-\\frac{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{x}_{n})-2{x}_{n})}{(-16\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}_{n})-2)}={x}_{n}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{x}_{n})+{x}_{n}}{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}_{n})+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nStarting with ${x}_{0}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={x}_{0}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{x}_{0})+{x}_{0}}{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}_{0})+1} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot 1)+1}{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot 1)+1} \\\\  & =0.878\\,555…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second iteration, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={x}_{1}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4{x}_{1})+{x}_{1}}{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4{x}_{1})+1} \\\\  & =(0.878\\,555…)-\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4(0.878\\,555…))+0.878\\,555…}{8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4(0.878\\,555…))+1} \\\\  & =0.901\\,873…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${x}_{1}≈0.879$ and ${x}_{2}≈0.902,$ rounded to three decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
